      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IM DUSTEE (2) was yet again about the mark last start when runner-up at this venue, beaten 1.6 metres. This is a little stronger but he should enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position and looks close to a win. MASON JOLIE (7) has been freshened since tackling the Vicbred series and had gone into that off a Cranbourne placing. Draws wide but is better placed at this level. OUR SWEET JEANNIE (1) has been coming from wider or second line barriers so is much better served by the ace draw. Has won two of three attempts at this circuit and distance so can turn the recent form around. MY ULTIMATE FRANCO NZ (5) must be included on the back of some solid recent form in NSW including a last-start placing at Wagga and a win last month at Cowra.",
